# The operator's own credentials and state. The Dockerfiles never COPY them —
# they are runtime mounts — but `docker build` sends the whole context to the
# daemon before the COPY filtering applies, so a remote or rootless buildx
# builder would otherwise receive the 2FA seeds under [auth.clients], the
# endpoint's private key, the relay bearer token and the admin token, and may
# keep them in its build cache.
config.toml
config/
secrets/
*.key
state.toml
*.admin-token
